    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 26,
    "summary": "Moses and Eleazar count the Israelites on the plains of Moab near Jericho—The males twenty years and older, excluding Levites, total 601,730—Only Caleb and Joshua remain from those numbered at Sinai.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass after the plague, that the Lord spake unto Moses and unto Eleazar the son of Aaron the priest, saying,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Numbers 26:1",
        "book": "Numbers",
        "chapter": 26,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "Take the sum of all the congregation of the children of Israel, from twenty years old and upward, throughout their fathers’ house, all that are able to go to war in Israel.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 5,
            "end": 8,
            "text": "OR a census by their fathers’ houses. Num. 1:2 (2–46)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Numbers 26:2",
        "book": "Numbers",
        "chapter": 26,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "And Moses and Eleazar the priest spake with them in the plains of Moab by Jordan near Jericho, saying,",
